  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nWrite a detailed description of the root cause and impact(s) of this finding.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nDescribe the best method(s) t#### Description\n\nIn `previewWithdraw`, the computation `inner = sub(PCMath.square(s), deduct)` underflows and reverts whenever `divUp(assets, HALF_SLOPE)` exceeds `square(totalShares)`. This occurs for any full withdrawal (`assets == totalAssets`) where the original deposit amount is not perfectly divisible in UD60x18 arithmetic — which is the overwhelmingly common case.\n\n**Root cause:** `square(s)` rounds **DOWN** (producing at most s²), while `divUp(assets, HALF_SLOPE)` rounds **UP** (producing at least assets/halfSlope). After a deposit where `div(assets, halfSlope)` had a non-zero remainder, the deposited assets encode more precision than `square(totalShares)` retains, causing `deduct > square(s)`.\n\nFees flowing into the vault via `_increaseProRataVaultAssets` (entry fees, exit fees) further inflate `totalAssets` without corresponding shares, widening the gap.\n\n#### Exploit Path\n\n1. Any user deposits assets where `assets * 1e18 % HALF_SLOPE != 0` (nearly all real-world deposits)\n2. Off-chain system or integrating contract calls `previewWithdraw(totalAssets, totalAssets, totalShares)`\n3. The call reverts with arithmetic underflow, breaking composability\n4. Also affects `OffsetProgressiveCurve` — instead of reverting, it silently returns `shares > totalShares` (off-by-one)o mitigate the finding.\n\n#### Recommended Fix\n\n```diff\n  function previewWithdraw(...) external view override returns (uint256 shares) {\n      _checkCurveDomains(totalAssets, totalShares, MAX_ASSETS, MAX_SHARES);\n      _checkWithdraw(assets, totalAssets);\n\n      UD60x18 s = wrap(totalShares);\n      UD60x18 deduct = PCMath.divUp(wrap(assets), HALF_SLOPE);\n+     UD60x18 sq = PCMath.square(s);\n+     UD60x18 inner = unwrap(deduct) >= unwrap(sq) ? wrap(0) : sub(sq, deduct);\n-     UD60x18 inner = sub(PCMath.square(s), deduct);\n      UD60x18 sharesUD = sub(s, sqrt(inner));\n      shares = unwrap(sharesUD);\n  }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "#### Proof of Concept\n\n**File:** `tests/PoCPreviewWithdraw.t.sol` — All 5 tests pass:\n```js\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport {Test, console2} from \"forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\nimport {TransparentUpgradeableProxy} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol\";\nimport {ProgressiveCurve} from \"src/protocol/curves/ProgressiveCurve.sol\";\nimport {OffsetProgressiveCurve} from \"src/protocol/curves/OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol\";\nimport {IBaseCurve} from \"src/interfaces/IBaseCurve.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title  PoC: previewWithdraw underflow / invalid return in Progressive Curves\n * @notice Demonstrates that previewWithdraw reverts (ProgressiveCurve) or returns\n *         shares > totalShares (OffsetProgressiveCurve) when withdrawing the full\n *         amount of assets deposited. Root cause: divUp rounds UP the deduction\n *         while square rounds DOWN the left-hand side, causing the intermediate\n *         subtraction to underflow.\n */\ncontract PoCPreviewWithdraw is Test {\n    ProgressiveCurve public progCurve;\n    OffsetProgressiveCurve public offsetCurve;\n\n    uint256 constant SLOPE = 2e18;\n    uint256 constant OFFSET = 1e18;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Deploy ProgressiveCurve\n        ProgressiveCurve progImpl = new ProgressiveCurve();\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy progProxy = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(\n            address(progImpl),\n            address(this),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(ProgressiveCurve.initialize.selector, \"ProgTest\", SLOPE)\n        );\n        progCurve = ProgressiveCurve(address(progProxy));\n\n        // Deploy OffsetProgressiveCurve\n        OffsetProgressiveCurve offsetImpl = new OffsetProgressiveCurve();\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy offsetProxy = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(\n            address(offsetImpl),\n            address(this),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(OffsetProgressiveCurve.initialize.selector, \"OffsetTest\", SLOPE, OFFSET)\n        );\n        offsetCurve = OffsetProgressiveCurve(address(offsetProxy));\n    }\n\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    //  FINDING 1: ProgressiveCurve.previewWithdraw reverts on full withdrawal\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    function test_POC_progressiveCurve_previewWithdraw_underflows_fullWithdrawal() public {\n        // Step 1 — Simulate a first deposit that creates rounding residue.\n        //          Deposit 5 ETH from totalShares=0.\n        uint256 depositAssets = 5e18;\n        uint256 shares = progCurve.previewDeposit(depositAssets, 0, 0);\n        console2.log(\"Deposit 5e18 assets -> shares:\", shares);\n\n        // After deposit: totalAssets = 5e18, totalShares = shares\n        uint256 totalAssets = depositAssets;\n        uint256 totalShares = shares;\n\n        // Step 2 — Verify previewRedeem works fine (it does not use the vulnerable path)\n        uint256 assetsBack = progCurve.previewRedeem(totalShares, totalShares, totalAssets);\n        console2.log(\"previewRedeem(all shares) -> assets:\", assetsBack);\n        assertLe(assetsBack, totalAssets, \"Redeem should return <= totalAssets\");\n\n        // Step 3 — Call previewWithdraw for the FULL totalAssets.\n        //          This REVERTS due to arithmetic underflow in sub(square(s), deduct).\n        vm.expectRevert(); // Solidity 0.8.29 checked-math underflow\n        progCurve.previewWithdraw(totalAssets, totalAssets, totalShares);\n    }\n\n    function test_POC_progressiveCurve_previewWithdraw_underflows_smallDeposit() public {\n        // Even a deposit of (1 ETH + 1 wei) triggers the bug\n        uint256 depositAssets = 1e18 + 1;\n        uint256 shares = progCurve.previewDeposit(depositAssets, 0, 0);\n        console2.log(\"Deposit 1e18+1 assets -> shares:\", shares);\n\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        progCurve.previewWithdraw(depositAssets, depositAssets, shares);\n    }\n\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    //  FINDING 2: OffsetProgressiveCurve.previewWithdraw returns shares > totalShares\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    function test_POC_offsetCurve_previewWithdraw_returnsSharesTooHigh() public {\n        // Step 1 — First deposit\n        uint256 depositAssets = 5e18;\n        uint256 shares = offsetCurve.previewDeposit(depositAssets, 0, 0);\n        console2.log(\"[Offset] Deposit 5e18 assets -> shares:\", shares);\n\n        uint256 totalAssets = depositAssets;\n        uint256 totalShares = shares;\n\n        // Step 2 — previewWithdraw returns shares > totalShares (silent corruption)\n        uint256 sharesNeeded = offsetCurve.previewWithdraw(totalAssets, totalAssets, totalShares);\n        console2.log(\"[Offset] previewWithdraw(totalAssets) -> shares:\", sharesNeeded);\n        console2.log(\"[Offset] totalShares:                          \", totalShares);\n\n        // This assertion demonstrates the bug: sharesNeeded > totalShares\n        assertGt(sharesNeeded, totalShares, \"BUG: previewWithdraw returns more shares than exist\");\n    }\n\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    //  Contrast: previewRedeem (the safe path) always works\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    function test_POC_previewRedeem_worksForFullRedemption() public {\n        uint256 depositAssets = 5e18;\n        uint256 shares = progCurve.previewDeposit(depositAssets, 0, 0);\n\n        // previewRedeem with all shares — works fine, rounds down\n        uint256 assetsBack = progCurve.previewRedeem(shares, shares, depositAssets);\n        console2.log(\"previewRedeem(all shares) -> assets back:\", assetsBack);\n        assertLe(assetsBack, depositAssets);\n        assertGt(assetsBack, 0);\n    }\n\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    //  Edge case: Deposit that divides cleanly does NOT trigger the bug\n    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    function test_POC_cleanDivisibleDeposit_noUnderflow() public view {\n        // 4e18 / halfSlope(1e18) = 4.0 exactly — no remainder, no rounding error\n        uint256 depositAssets = 4e18;\n        uint256 shares = progCurve.previewDeposit(depositAssets, 0, 0);\n        console2.log(\"Clean deposit 4e18 -> shares:\", shares);\n\n        // This does NOT revert because sqrt(4) = 2 exactly in UD60x18\n        uint256 sharesNeeded = progCurve.previewWithdraw(depositAssets, depositAssets, shares);\n        console2.log(\"previewWithdraw(4e18) -> shares:\", sharesNeeded);\n        assertEq(sharesNeeded, shares, \"Clean case: full withdrawal works\");\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n```\nforge test --match-contract PoCPreviewWithdraw -vvv\n\n[PASS] test_POC_progressiveCurve_previewWithdraw_underflows_fullWithdrawal()\n       -- Deposit 5e18 -> previewWithdraw(5e18) REVERTS (arithmetic underflow)\n\n[PASS] test_POC_progressiveCurve_previewWithdraw_underflows_smallDeposit()\n       -- Even 1e18+1 triggers the bug\n\n[PASS] test_POC_offsetCurve_previewWithdraw_returnsSharesTooHigh()\n       -- previewWithdraw returns 1449489742783178099 but totalShares = 1449489742783178098 (off-by-one)\n\n[PASS] test_POC_previewRedeem_worksForFullRedemption()\n       -- Contrast: previewRedeem works fine (rounds down safely)\n\n[PASS] test_POC_cleanDivisibleDeposit_noUnderflow()\n       -- 4e18 deposit divides cleanly -> no bug (confirms root cause is rounding)\n```",
